      f: push rbp; mov rbp,rsp; sub rsp,0x20
         mov rax,[rdi+0x78]
         pxor xmm0,xmm0; movaps [rbp-0x20],xmm0
         test rax,rax; je 3f
         mov rdx,[rax+8]; mov rsi,[rax+0x10]
         movq xmm0,rdx; movq xmm4,rsi; punpcklqdq xmm0,xmm4
         movaps [rbp-0x20],xmm0
      1: cmp qword [rdi+0xe0],0; je 2f
         sub rsi,[rdi+0x50]; mov [rbp-0x18],rsi
      2: lea rdi,[rbp-0x20]; call g; leave; ret
      3: xor esi,esi; xor edx,edx; jmp 1b

    This is the shape of _dl_relocate_object in the mcount_x86_64 fixture.
    The merge intersection test asks whether the 8-byte constant 0 in rsi is a
    partial copy shadow of the 16-byte constant 0 at byte offset 8.
    Varnode::findSubpieceShadow answered by shifting the 64-bit constant right
    by 64 bits: a panic in a build with overflow checks (the function printed
    as an empty body with a failure warning), an unreported wrapped shift
    count otherwise.  A constant wider than 8 bytes holds zero above bit 63,
    so the truncation now reads 0 there.

    Stage / sub-stage: P6 merge (cover intersection, partial copy shadow),
    always on.
